do_1 = "Reconcile the task, requirement and acceptance blocks in spec/layerx-merge/programme/issues/1802.kvx:18, :40 and :45 and spec/layerx-merge/programme/issues/1803.kvx:19, :41 and :46, together with their integrated counterparts in spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:160015, :159985, :25392, :25388, :335727 and :335719: include the exact statement Absent or empty publishable keys return null before endpoint or RPC validation. and require that result for absent, empty, whitespace-only and configured endpoints; server rendering returns null regardless of key or endpoint; a nonempty key with an absent, empty or whitespace-only endpoint throws an error naming NEXT_PUBLIC_PAXEER_WALLET_API, and a configured endpoint is trimmed and used with the existing chain and RPC precedence. Remove the prescribed empty-browser assert.rejects and rejection acceptance from the 1803 plan, while preserving explicit endpoint configuration with no default under decision 2755 at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:9645 and the injected-connector coverage in the 1802 plan."
do_2 = "Update dependency and gate declarations at spec/layerx-merge/programme/issues/1803.kvx:13 and :23 and spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:159979 and :159989 so task 18.1803.1 requires 18.1802.1 in addition to the existing 22.39.234 type-resolution prerequisite and occupies the next wave; reflect that prerequisite in the report as well, and retain task 18.1802.1's focused repair-file verification until the old regression is updated. The final 1803 verify_cmd must be pnpm --dir apps/perps exec node --test --test-concurrency=1 --import tsx --test-name-pattern '^(chainIdFromChainObject|disabled_embedded_wallet_keeps_injected_connector|missing_endpoint_refuses_with_the_setting_name|configured_endpoint_is_used_by_the_embedded_client)$' tests/embedded-wallet.test.ts tests/repair-22-31-603.test.ts, with all four cases listed in tests. Preserve the existing enabled-wallet refusal and configured-client assertions at apps/perps/tests/repair-22-31-603.test.ts:37 and :49 and require the named chainIdFromChainObject function planned at spec/layerx-merge/programme/issues/1803.kvx:18."
do_3 = "Keep the runtime fixes owned by tasks 18.1802.1 and 18.1803.1, update their continuation instructions at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:160034 and :160004 to apply the reconciled contract rather than retain contradictory assertions, and retain qualification UNRUN until their declared gates actually pass with revision, command, exit and private log evidence; no runtime gate result is inferred from this documentation repair. Verify both reports with their existing checker and check the shared matrix, removal of the contradictory rejection and inclusion of the disabled-wallet case in the final combined selector."
